The diagram shows the graph of $y = f'(x)$, the derivative of a function $y = f(x)$. Which statement about $y = f(x)$ is correct?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
             xmin=-4.4, xmax=6.4, ymin=-6.8, ymax=10.8, samples=100, clip=false,
             xtick={-4,-3,-2,-1,1,2,3,4,5,6}, ytick={-6,-4,-2,2,4,6,8,10}]
\addplot[smooth, thick, <->, domain=-2.87:4.87] {-x*x + 2*x + 8};
\node[font=\small] at (axis cs:4.4,6) {$y=f'(x)$};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
